WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.540
Fisherman rib is a beautiful ribber

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:06.460
technique that incorporates
tuck on both needle beds.

3
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:11.820
For machines that have this ribber
carriage, it can be problematic to knit

4
00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:17.740
fisherman rib, but it's not impossible.
If you've used other knitting machines

5
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.780
this feature of this machine
is a little different.

6
00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:27.500
Take a moment to explore how this
carriage works on your machine.

7
00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.180
Disconnect the ribber carriage

8
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:34.460
from the coupler and move the main
bed carriage out of the way.

9
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:38.540
Pull a few needles all
the way out to hold position.

10
00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.540
Pass the carriage back and forth.

11
00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:44.680
Notice that the needles do not engage. No

12
00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.700
matter what knitting you
have on the ribber carriage.

13
00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.140
Those needles do not move.

14
00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:58.040
Look at the side of the carriage and
locate this small, somewhat hidden lever.

15
00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:04.410
Hold the lever up with your finger or
a tool and slowly pass the carriage across

16
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:11.120
the needles and you'll see that the
needles engage and they will now knit.

17
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.100
Looking at the underside of the carriage
will give you a visual of this.

18
00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:21.660
With the levers in their default position,
the needle butts travel through this

19
00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:27.260
neutral channel and they're
not going to move or knit.

20
00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:30.260
But by forcing the needle butts through

21
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:36.210
this channel with the little lever,
the needles will now knit

22
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.980
now just as a point of interest.

23
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.380
While we're looking at the underside

24
00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.930
of the carriage,
when the needles are in working or middle

25
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:50.060
position, they'll travel through these
channels for regular knitting and slip.

26
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:54.020
So how do you work fisherman
rib on this machine?

27
00:01:54.050 --> 00:02:00.760
Cast on for 1x1 ribbing.
End with your carriage on the right.

28
00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.780
Set your main bed carriage
to tuck or hold to the left.

29
00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:09.220
By setting the left Cam lever to H.

30
00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:14.890
It's going to remain in this position.
So your left Cam lever is at H.

31
00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:21.520
Your right Cam lever is at N for regular
knitting on your main bed carriage.

32
00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:28.200
Next, set the ribber for plain knitting.

33
00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.700
Work the setup row.

34
00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:41.120
Pull  the main bed needles all the way out
to hold position and knit to the left.

35
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:48.560
The main bed needles will tuck
and the ribber needles will knit.

36
00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:54.340
The stitch pattern is worked
in two steps over two rows.

37
00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:59.380
Step one, you've got your
carriage on your left.

38
00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:04.280
Pull the ribber needles all
the way out to hold position.

39
00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.540
Knit to the right.

40
00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:13.400
Remember, the main bed is
set to knit to the right.

41
00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:21.660
Step two, with the carriage on the right,
pull the main bed needles out to hold.

42
00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:25.840
Now notice now all
the needles are out to hold.

43
00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:32.260
But this time we're going to force those
held ribber needles to knit by holding

44
00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:36.820
that little side lever up so it
clears the butts of the needles.

45
00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.500
When you knit to the left,

46
00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:45.360
those ribbing needles are going to knit
and the main bed needles will hold.

47
00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:51.120
Repeat steps one and two
for the length of your knitting.

48
00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.380
Let's go back to step one.

49
00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.420
The carriage is on the left.

50
00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:01.080
Pull the ribber needles all the way out
to hold position so all your needles are

51
00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:05.860
in hold position, but your main
bed is set to knit to the right.

52
00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:10.500
Knit to the right, your main bed
needles knit. Your ribber needles

53
00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.120
hold. Step two.

54
00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.500
Your carriage is on the right.

55
00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:19.060
Pull all the main bed
needles to hold. Again,

56
00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:22.680
all those needles are in hold.

57
00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:29.460
Force those held ribbing needles
to knit by holding the side lever up,

58
00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.620
knit to the left.

59
00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:37.480
The main bed needles will hold
the ribbing needles will knit.

60
00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:43.020
Continue to do this for the
length of your knitting.

61
00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.240
Now notice that you're not changing any

62
00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:50.860
carriage settings as you're knitting
except for holding that little lever up.

63
00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:54.920
When you want the ribber needles to knit.

64
00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.140
Something to keep in mind.

65
00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.700
If you're knitting with your ribber

66
00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:05.980
and you want to work short rows,
this little lever comes into play again.

67
00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:12.180
The only way to get needles that are all
the way out on the ribber to knit is

68
00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:18.700
to hold that little lever up and force
the needle butts through the channel

69
00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.140
so the needles will knit.

70
00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.340
Knitting fisherman Rib
on this machine isn't hard.

71
00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.820
It's just different than other machines.

72
00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.380
Have fun with Fisherman.

73
00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.480
Rib Other Ribbing variations.

